<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann Lukas von Hildebrandt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1668–1745</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann Lukas von Hildebrandt was an Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> architect, born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>, who became court architect in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>. His masterpiece is the Belvedere, built for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-eugene-of-savoy">Prince Eugene of Savoy</a> between 1714 and 1723, and he also worked on the Schwarzenberg Palace in Vienna and the rebuilding of Göttweig Abbey. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-bernhard-fischer-von-erlach">Johann Bernhard Fischer von Erlach</a> he shaped the Viennese Baroque style.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johann-lukas-von-hildebrandt.jpg" alt="Johann Lukas von Hildebrandt" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacob van Schuppen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johann_Lucas_von_Hildebrandt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
